            <ArticleTitle>Lipoprotein subspecies and risk of coronary disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>B78-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This review summarizes physical and chemical properties of major subspecies of very-low-, low-, intermediate, and high-density lipoproteins. Hypotheses regarding the metabolic origins of these subspecies and evidence for their associations with risk of coronary artery disease are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
